window.FluentComparison = {"rows": [{"id": "paper-title", "kind": "title", "sources": [], "html": "<h1 class=\"title\">Swing-up control of double-inverted pendulum systems<\/h1>", "translation_html": "\n<p>二重倒立振り子系のスイングアップ制御<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "abstract-p1-b7", "kind": "abstract", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b7", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.12, 0.366, 0.878, 0.521]}], "html": "<p>\n\n    This article deals with presenting a new swing-up control approach of a double-inverted pendulum on a trolley. The dynamic model of the double-inverted pendulum is derived and linearized. Two different linearization approaches are used: first, the traditional Taylor’s series approach and, second, using partial linearization. A state feedback control algorithm has been implemented based on the linearized model from Taylor’s series. Furthermore, a method for swinging up the pendulum to the inversion position from rest (swing-up) has been presented. The design and implementation of the swing-up function of the pendulum are implemented using the partial linearized model. The swing-up control procedure depends on using the feedforward–feedback controllers’ combination to transfer the pendulums from the downward to the upward position. The time-variant controller gain is used for the sake of the swing-up control procedure. The performances of these algorithms are shown in this paper through simulations.\n  <\/p>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本論文では、トロリー上に配置された二重反転振り子の新たなスイングアップ制御手法について述べる。二重反転振り子の動的モデルを導出し、線形化する。線形化手法として、まず従来のテイラー級数法を、次に部分線形化法を用いる。テイラー級数による線形化モデルに基づき、状態フィードバック制御アルゴリズムを実装した。さらに、静止状態から振り子を反転位置へとスイングアップさせる手法（スイングアップ）を提示する。振り子のスイングアップ関数の設計および実装には、部分線形化モデルを用いる。スイングアップ制御手順では、フィードフォワード・フィードバック制御器の組み合わせを用いて、振り子を下方位置から上方位置へと遷移させる。スイングアップ制御手順においては、時変制御器ゲインを用いる。これらのアルゴリズムの性能を、本論文ではシミュレーションを通じて示す。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p1-b4", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b4", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.155, 0.26, 0.843, 0.308]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"1\">\n<p><sup>1<\/sup>Biomedical Engineering Department, Al-Mustaqbal University College, Hillah, Iraq <sup>2<\/sup>Department of Mechanical Engineering, University of Babylon, College of Engineering, Hillah, Iraq <sup>3<\/sup>Department of Biomedical Engineering, University of Babylon, College of Engineering, Hillah, Iraq<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p><sup>1<\/sup>アル・ムスタクバル大学カレッジ\n生体医工学学科、イラク・ヒラー <sup>2<\/sup>バビロン大学\n機械工学科、工学部、イラク・ヒラー <sup>3<\/sup>バビロン大学\n生体医工学学科、工学部、イラク・ヒラー<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p1-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b5", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.198, 0.313, 0.799, 0.33]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"1\">\n<p><strong>Correspondence:<\/strong> Ameen M. Al Juboori (ameenal-juboori@mustaqbal-college.edu.iq)<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p><strong>問い合わせ先：<\/strong> アミーン・M・アル・ジュブーリ\n(ameenal-juboori@mustaqbal-college.edu.iq)<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p1-b6", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b6", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.148, 0.339, 0.85, 0.354]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"1\">\n<p>Received: 25 November 2022 – Revised: 4 May 2023 – Accepted: 9 November 2023 – Published: 29 January 2024<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>受理：2022年11月25日 – 改訂：2023年5月4日 – 採択：2023年11月9日 –\n公開：2024年1月29日<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p1-b8", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b8", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.075, 0.557, 0.197, 0.572]}], "html": "<h2 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p1-b8\">1 Introduction<\/h2>", "translation_html": "\n<p>1 はじめに<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p1-b9", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b9", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.072, 0.598, 0.487, 0.92]}, {"id": "p1-b10", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.511, 0.557, 0.923, 0.588]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"1\">\n<p>Non-linear, unstable, or underactuated systems are generally very difficult to control. Therefore, they are considered to be a challenge and are the subject of many technical reports, student projects, and academic papers. Their goal is not always to build a practically useful device but rather to develop or improve existing control algorithms, either by simulation or even experimentally to verify their applicability in general. The double-inverted pendulum model consists of several parts. A cart moves along a linear track, and two pendulums are connected to the carriage and each other by a rotational linkage (Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-1\">1<\/a>). The input to the system is the torque of a DC motor, which is transmitted by a toothed belt as a force to the carriage. The system has one challenging equilibrium position in which the system can be stabilized, the upper (inverse) (see Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-1\">1<\/a>a–c). Furthermore, three configurations of the double-inverted pendulum, which are upperlower, lower-upper, and lower, are also considered as equilibrium positions. the lower equilibrium is always reached by the system (with the damping element) in finite time; control is needed to maintain the upper-lower, lower-upper, and inverse configurations in real conditions. The stabilization of the double-inverse pendulum is further understood in this paper as a regulation to maintain its inverse position.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>非線形、不安定、あるいは過小駆動なシステムは、一般に制御が非常に困難である。そのため、これらは課題と見なされており、多くの技術報告書や学生プロジェクト、学術論文の題材となっている。その目的は、必ずしも実用的に有用な装置を構築することではなく、むしろ既存の制御アルゴリズムを開発または改良し、シミュレーションや、さらには実験的にその汎用性を検証することにある。二重反転振り子モデルは、複数の構成要素から成る。台車が直線軌道上を走行し、2つの振り子が回転リンク機構によって台車および互いに接続されている（図<a href=\"#fig-1\">1<\/a>）。システムへの入力はDCモータのトルクであり、これが歯付きベルトを介して力として台車に伝達される。本システムには、安定させることができる困難な平衡位置が1つあり、それは上側（反転）位置である（図<a href=\"#fig-1\">1<\/a>a–c参照）。さらに、上下、下上、および下という二重反転振り子の3つの構成も平衡位置として考えられる。下側の平衡位置には、（減衰要素を備えた）システムが常に有限時間で到達するが、実環境において上下、下上、および反転の各構成を維持するには制御が必要となる。本論文では、二重反転振り子の安定化を、反転位置を維持するための調節としてさらに捉えている。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p1-b11", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b11", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.51, 0.588, 0.925, 0.74]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"1\">\n<p>The next task of the control program is to be the so-called swing-up. This term refers to the realization of such a movement of the carriage that brings the system from the lower equilibrium position to the inverse position. The situation is indicated in Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-1\">1<\/a>c. The control requirement is primarily for the robustness and repeatability of the swing-up. There are several published articles with different methods addressing the swing-up problem of a double-inverted pendulum. However, in the vast majority of cases, these are only simulations that have not been experimentally verified on a real system.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>制御プログラムの次の課題は、いわゆるスイングアップである。この用語は、システムを下側の平衡位置から逆位置へと移行させる、台車のこのような動作の実現を指す。その状況を図<a href=\"#fig-1\">1<\/a>cに示す。制御上の要件は、主にスイングアップのロバスト性と再現性にある。二重倒立振り子のスイングアップ問題に取り組んだ異なる手法による論文がいくつか発表されている。しかし、その大部分は実機で実験的に検証されていないシミュレーションに過ぎない。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p1-b12", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p1-b12", "page": 1, "bbox": [0.51, 0.741, 0.926, 0.91]}, {"id": "p2-b3", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.072, 0.354, 0.487, 0.477]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"1\">\n<p>A mathematical model of this system was derived based on the Lagrangian mechanics; the dynamic model is discretized, and then the Laguerre series is implemented in model pre-dictive control technology to trace the control signal for the system <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-12\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-12\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Qian et al., 2011<\/a>)<\/span>. An RNA genetic algorithm with fuzzy logic is used to control the pendulum system, where the fuzzy logic controller can improve the performance of the controller by using the RNA genetic algorithm to find certain optimal membership functions <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-13\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-13\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Sun et al., 2015<\/a>)<\/span>. The technical report compares the linear quadratic regulator, the state-dependent Riccati equation (SDRE), and the use of neural networks (NNs) and concludes that the NNs have a limited capability to improve the SDRE performance <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-2\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-2\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Bogdanov, 2004<\/a>)<\/span>. Adaptive sliding-mode control in combination with a fuzzy neural network is used to control a double-inverted pendulum. The fuzzy neural network is designed as a system controller, and the adaptive sliding mode is designed to carry out the disturbance problem <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-9\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-9\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Mon and Lin, 2014<\/a>)<\/span>.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ラグランジュ力学に基づき、本システムの数理モデルを導出した。動的モデルを離散化し、次いでラゲール級数をモデルの事前予測制御技術に実装することで、システム<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-12\">2011<\/a>の制御信号を追跡した。ファジィ論理を用いたRNA遺伝的アルゴリズムにより振り子システムを制御し、当該ファジィ論理コントローラは、RNA遺伝的アルゴリズムを用いて特定の最適メンバーシップ関数<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-13\">Sun et al.,\n2015<\/a>を求めることで、コントローラの性能を向上させることができる。本技術報告書では、線形二次レギュレータ、状態依存リカタ方程式（SDRE）、およびニューラルネットワーク（NN）の利用を比較し、NNによるSDREの性能向上能力には限界があると結論付けている<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-2\">Bogdanov,\n2004<\/a>。ファジィニューラルネットワークを組み合わせた適応型スライディングモード制御を用いて、二重反転振り子を制御する。ファジィニューラルネットワークをシステムコントローラとして設計し、適応型スライディングモードを外乱問題の解決に向けて設計している<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-9\">Mon and Lin, 2014<\/a>。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b4", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b4", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.072, 0.477, 0.487, 0.812]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>In the previous literature, the dynamic model of the double-inverted pendulum system is linearized around an operating point to design a linear controller. An alternative to the above dynamic linearization is partial feedback linearization – splitting the generalized coordinates into a regularization whose dimensions are given by the number of inputs, and variables consider only zero dynamics <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-5 paper-ref-10\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>; <a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-10\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Neusser and Valášek, 2013<\/a>)<\/span>. This path of linearization is used to design the swing-up function of the double-inverted pendulum <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-5\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>)<\/span>. A more detailed description of the method can be found in the swing-up control practical example <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-10\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-10\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Neusser and Valášek, 2013<\/a>)<\/span>. Swing-up control of the double-inverted system was proposed to separate pendulums and to control each one distinctly <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-6\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-6\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Henmi et al., 2014<\/a>)<\/span>. A non-linear model predictive control is used to build up a control algorithm for swingup motion <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-8\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-8\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Jaiwat and Ohtsuka, 2014<\/a>)<\/span>. A method for controlling the energy of the system with partial linearization is presented, and passivity-based control is utilized in the work <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-14\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-14\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Zhong and Rock, 2001<\/a>)<\/span>. The solution of the boundary value problem with free parameters is used to generate the control approach <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-4\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-4\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Graichen et al., 2007<\/a>)<\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>先行文献では、線形制御器を設計するために、二重倒立振り子系の動的モデルを動作点まわりで線形化している。上述の動的線形化に代わる手法として部分フィードバック線形化があり、これは一般化座標を、入力数によって与えられる次元を持つ正則化に分割し、変数としてゼロダイナミクス\n<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>; <a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-10\">Neusser and Valášek, 2013<\/a>\nのみを考慮するものである。この線形化手法を用いて、二重倒立振り子のスイングアップ関数\n<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>\nを設計する。本手法のより詳細な説明は、スイングアップ制御の実用例 <a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-10\">Neusser and Valášek, 2013<\/a>\nに記載されている。二重倒立系のスイングアップ制御は、振り子を分離し、それぞれを個別に制御するために提案された\n<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-6\">Henmi et al.,\n2014<\/a>。非線形モデル予測制御を用いて、スイングアップ動作のための制御アルゴリズムを構築している\n<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-8\">Jaiwat and Ohtsuka,\n2014<\/a>。部分線形化による系のエネルギー制御手法が提示されており、本研究では受動性に基づく制御が活用されている\n<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-14\">Zhong and Rock,\n2001<\/a>。自由パラメータを持つ境界値問題の解法を用いて、制御手法が構築されている\n<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-4\">2007<\/a>。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b5", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.072, 0.812, 0.487, 0.92]}, {"id": "p2-b6", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.509, 0.081, 0.925, 0.264]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>The motivation of this work was mainly to demonstrate the theoretical swing-up control procedures on a model of a double-inverted pendulum. Indeed, there are not many publications that deal with the application of the proposed algorithms on a real mechanism. The paper focuses on the theoretical basis for the following part. It consists of an explanation of the terms used and a search of the studied area in terms of stabilization and swing-up. It also includes the derivation of the equations of motion and the presentation of the existing double-pendulum model. Furthermore, this study serves to apply a linear quadratic controller and a Kalman filter and lastly to implement the swing-up function. The boundary value problem is solved to generate the trajectory for the swing-up motion of the pendulums. The partial linear realization method is used to linearize the system dynamically during the swing-up process. Dynamic input–output decoupling is used to keep the system in a stable position after the pendulums reach the upper unstable position <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-12\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-12\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Qian et al., 2011<\/a>)<\/span>.<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本研究の主目的は、二重倒立振り子のモデルを用いて、理論的なスイングアップ制御手順を実証することであった。実際、提案したアルゴリズムを実際の機構に適用した研究論文は多くない。本論文では、後続部分の理論的基盤に焦点を当てる。具体的には、使用した用語の解説と、安定化およびスイングアップの観点からの検討領域の探索を行う。また、運動方程式の導出および既存の二重振り子モデルの提示も行う。さらに、本研究では線形二次制御器とカルマンフィルタを適用し、最終的にスイングアップ機能を実装する。境界値問題を解くことで、振り子のスイングアップ運動の軌道を生成する。スイングアップ過程において、システムを動的に線形化するために部分線形実現法を用いる。振り子が上部の不安定位置<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-12\">2011<\/a>に到達した後、システムを安定な状態に維持するため、動的な入出力デカップリングを採用する。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b7", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b7", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.509, 0.263, 0.924, 0.341]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>The rest of the paper is organized as follows: in the following section, the mathematical model is derived; next, the stabilization control is presented; after that, the swing-up procedure is detailed; later, the simulation of the work is addressed, and the article conclusions are shown in the last section.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本論文の構成は以下の通りである。次節では数理モデルを導出し、続いて安定化制御を提示し、その後スイングアップ手順について詳述する。さらにその後、計算機シミュレーションについて述べ、最終節で論文の結論を示す。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p2-b8", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b8", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.51, 0.359, 0.719, 0.375]}], "html": "<h2 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p2-b8\">2 Mathematical modeling<\/h2>", "translation_html": "\n<p>2 数理モデリング<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b9", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b9", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.508, 0.388, 0.926, 0.511]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>Figure <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-2\">2<\/a> schematically shows the double-inverted pendulum model. The meaning of the individual variables is evident from the figure. The system has 3 degrees of freedom – the sliding motion of the carriage and the rotational motions of the two pendulums. A vector of state variables is constructed as the displacement of the carriage or the rotation of the pendulums and the velocity of the carriage or the angular velocity of the pendulums:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>図<a href=\"#fig-2\">2<\/a>は、二重倒立振り子モデルを模式的に示したものである。個々の変数の意味は図から明らかである。本系は、台車の摺動運動と2つの振り子の回転運動という3つの自由度を持つ。状態変数のベクトルは、台車の変位または振り子の回転、および台車の速度または振り子の角速度として構成される：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b10", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b10", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.511, 0.52, 0.922, 0.542]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_1_equation_11.jpg\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\boldsymbol {\\theta} = \\left[ \\theta_ {0}, \\theta_ {1}, \\theta_ {2}, \\dot {\\theta} _ {0}, \\dot {\\theta} _ {1}, \\dot {\\theta} _ {2} \\right] ^ {T}.\n\\tag{1}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p2-b11", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b11", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.51, 0.55, 0.924, 0.583]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>For input u, the problem of obtaining a mathematical model is a search for an equation of motion of the following form:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>入力 u\nに対して、数理モデルを求める問題とは、次のような形式の運動方程式を求めることである：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b12", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b12", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.511, 0.592, 0.922, 0.61]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_1_equation_13.jpg\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\dot {\\boldsymbol {\\theta}} = \\boldsymbol {f} (\\boldsymbol {\\theta}) + \\boldsymbol {g} (\\boldsymbol {\\theta} u).\n\\tag{2}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p2-b13", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b13", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.51, 0.62, 0.924, 0.699]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>Lagrange’s equations of the second kind were used for this purpose. The mathematical model of the double-inverse pendulum can be expressed as the sum of or difference between the partial derivatives of the mechanical energies according to the respective independent variables and their derivatives:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>この目的には、ラグランジュの第2種方程式が用いられた。二重逆振り子の数学的モデルは、それぞれの独立変数およびそれらの導関数による力学的エネルギーの偏微分の和または差として表現できる：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b14", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b14", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.512, 0.708, 0.921, 0.747]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_1_equation_15.jpg\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\frac {\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d} t} \\left(\\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {E} _ {K}}{\\dot {\\boldsymbol {\\theta}} _ {i}}\\right) - \\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {E} _ {K}}{\\boldsymbol {\\theta} _ {i}} + \\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {D}}{\\boldsymbol {\\theta} _ {i}} + \\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {E} _ {P}}{\\boldsymbol {\\theta} _ {i}} = \\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {W} _ {\\mathrm{e}}}{\\boldsymbol {\\theta} _ {i}} = \\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {P} _ {e}}{\\dot {\\boldsymbol {\\theta}} _ {i}},\n\\tag{3}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p2-b15", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b15", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.51, 0.757, 0.924, 0.834]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>where <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{K}}\\)<\/span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathrm{E_p}\\)<\/span> are the kinetic and the potential energy. D denotes the dissipative component, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(W_{e}\\)<\/span> denotes the work of external forces, and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(P_{\\mathrm{e}}\\)<\/span> denotes their power. For individual bodies, the kinetic, potential, and dissipative energies and external forces can be expressed <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-2\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-2\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Bogdanov, 2004<\/a>)<\/span>.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{K}}\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathrm{E_p}\\)<\/span>は運動エネルギーと位置エネルギーである。Dは散逸成分を、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(W_{e}\\)<\/span>は外力の仕事量を、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(P_{\\mathrm{e}}\\)<\/span>はその仕事率を表す。個々の物体については、運動エネルギー、位置エネルギー、散逸エネルギー、および外力を<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-2\">Bogdanov, 2004<\/a>で表すことができる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b16", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b16", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.51, 0.834, 0.924, 0.88]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p>The velocity energies of the centers of gravity of the pendulums can be obtained from the time derivative of their position vector.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>振り子の重心の速度エネルギーは、その位置ベクトルの時間微分から求めることができる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p2-b17", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p2-b17", "page": 2, "bbox": [0.512, 0.885, 0.922, 0.921]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_1_equation_18.jpg\" data-source-page=\"2\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nE _ {\\mathrm{K} _ {0}} = \\frac {1}{2} m _ {0} \\dot {\\theta} _ {0} ^ {2} + \\frac {1}{2} I _ {0} \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} = \\frac {1}{2} m _ {0} \\dot {\\theta} _ {0} ^ {2} + \\frac {1}{2} \\frac {I _ {0}}{R _ {0} ^ {2}} \\dot {\\theta} _ {0} ^ {2}\n\\tag{4}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b3", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b3", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.074, 0.33, 0.483, 0.36]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_4.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nE _ {\\mathrm{K} _ {1}} = \\frac {1}{2} m _ {1} \\left[ \\left(\\dot {\\theta} _ {0} + l _ {1} \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} \\cos \\theta_ {1}\\right) ^ {2} + \\left(l _ {1} \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} \\sin \\theta_ {1}\\right) ^ {2} \\right] + \\frac {1}{2} l _ {1} \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} ^ {2}\n\\tag{5}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b4", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b4", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.074, 0.379, 0.483, 0.442]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_5.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{c} E _ {\\mathrm{K} _ {2}} = \\frac {1}{2} m _ {2} \\Big [ \\big (\\dot {\\theta} _ {0} + L _ {1} \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} \\cos \\theta_ {1} + l _ {2} \\dot {\\theta} _ {2} \\cos \\theta_ {2} \\big) ^ {2} \\\\ \\quad + \\big (L _ {1} \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} \\sin \\theta_ {1} + l _ {2} \\dot {\\theta} _ {2} \\sin \\theta_ {2} \\big) ^ {2} \\Big ] + \\frac {1}{2} I _ {2} \\dot {\\theta} _ {2} ^ {2} \\end{array}\n\\tag{6}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b5", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.074, 0.447, 0.282, 0.463]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>Potential energy is as follows:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ポテンシャルエネルギーは以下の通りです。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b6", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b6", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.074, 0.47, 0.483, 0.506]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_7.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{c} E _ {P _ {0}} = 0, E _ {P _ {1}} = m _ {1} g l _ {1} \\cos \\theta_ {1}, E _ {P _ {2}} \\\\ = m _ {2} g (L _ {1} \\cos \\theta_ {1} + l _ {2} \\cos \\theta_ {2}). \\end{array}\n\\tag{7}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b7", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b7", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.073, 0.514, 0.352, 0.53]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>The dissipative component is as follows:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>散逸成分は以下の通りである。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b8", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b8", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.074, 0.534, 0.483, 0.597]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_9.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{l} D _ {0} = \\frac {1}{2} b _ {0} \\dot {\\theta} _ {0} ^ {2}, D _ {1} = \\frac {1}{2} b _ {1} \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} ^ {2} + \\frac {1}{2} b _ {2} \\big (\\dot {\\theta} _ {2} - \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} \\big) ^ {2}, \\\\ D _ {2} = \\frac {1}{2} b _ {2} \\big (\\dot {\\theta} _ {2} - \\dot {\\theta} _ {1} \\big) ^ {2}. \\end{array}\n\\tag{8}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b9", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b9", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.073, 0.603, 0.486, 0.68]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>In Eqs. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-4\">4<\/a>)–(<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-8\">8<\/a>), the <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_{j}\\)<\/span> represents the motion variable; <span class=\"math inline\">\\(m_{j}\\)<\/span> is the mass; <span class=\"math inline\">\\(b_{j}\\)<\/span> is the viscous friction constant; and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(j = 0,1,2\\)<\/span> stands for cart and first and second pendulum, respectively. <span class=\"math inline\">\\(I_{0}\\)<\/span> is the inertia of the pulley, and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(l_{1,2}\\)<\/span> are the lengths of the pendulums.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>式(<a href=\"#eq-4\">4<\/a>)–(<a href=\"#eq-8\">8<\/a>)において、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_{j}\\)<\/span>は運動変数、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(m_{j}\\)<\/span>は質量、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(b_{j}\\)<\/span>は粘性摩擦定数、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(j =\n0,1,2\\)<\/span>はそれぞれ台車および第1・第2振り子を表す。<span class=\"math inline\">\\(I_{0}\\)<\/span>は滑車の慣性、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(l_{1,2}\\)<\/span>は振り子の長さである。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b10", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b10", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.072, 0.68, 0.487, 0.757]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>The only input to the system is the moment μ on the motor shaft. However, for better understanding, the equations were derived for the force on the carriage F. There is a simple relationship of direct proportionality between these two quantities:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>システムへの唯一の入力は、モータ軸上のモーメントμである。ただし、理解を深めるため、台車に作用する力Fについて方程式を導出した。これら2つの量の間には、単純な正比例の関係がある：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b11", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b11", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.074, 0.764, 0.483, 0.78]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_12.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\mu = F R _ {0},\n\\tag{9}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b12", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b12", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.073, 0.787, 0.485, 0.818]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>where <span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{0}\\)<\/span> is the radius of the pulley. Then the external force output is given by<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{0}\\)<\/span>はプーリーの半径である。このとき、外力の出力は次のように与えられる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b13", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b13", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.075, 0.824, 0.483, 0.841]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_14.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\boldsymbol {P} _ {\\mathrm{e}} = F \\dot {\\theta} _ {0}.\n\\tag{10}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b14", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b14", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.073, 0.849, 0.486, 0.895]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>Substituting the above equations into Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-2\">2<\/a>) gives the resulting equation of motion, which can be written in standard matrix form:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>上記の式を式(<a href=\"#eq-2\">2<\/a>)に代入すると、得られる運動方程式が得られ、これは標準的な行列形式で次のように記述できる：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b15", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b15", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.073, 0.903, 0.483, 0.919]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_16.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\mathbf {M} (\\boldsymbol {q}) \\ddot {\\boldsymbol {q}} + \\mathbf {B} (\\boldsymbol {q}, \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}}) \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}} + \\mathbf {K} (\\boldsymbol {q}) = \\boldsymbol {H} _ {u},\n\\tag{11}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b16", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b16", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.51, 0.081, 0.924, 0.127]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>where the vector <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q} = [\\theta_0,\\theta_1,\\theta_2]\\)<\/span> ; the introduction of matrices is not listed here for the sake of abbreviation. The equation of motion in the form of Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-5\">5<\/a>) can be expressed as follows:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここでベクトル <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q} =\n[\\theta_0,\\theta_1,\\theta_2]\\)<\/span>\nであり、簡略化のため行列の導入についてはここでは記載しない。式 (<a href=\"#eq-5\">5<\/a>) の形式による運動方程式は、次のように表される：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b17", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b17", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.511, 0.135, 0.922, 0.208]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_18.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{c} \\dot {\\boldsymbol {\\theta}} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c c} \\mathbf {0} &amp; \\mathbf {I} \\\\ \\mathbf {0} &amp; - \\mathbf {M} ^ {- 1} \\mathbf {B} \\end{array} \\right] \\boldsymbol {\\theta} + \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} \\mathbf {0} \\\\ - \\mathbf {M} ^ {- 1} \\mathbf {K} \\end{array} \\right] \\\\ + \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} 0 \\\\ \\mathbf {M} ^ {- 1} \\mathbf {H} \\end{array} \\right] u, \\end{array}\n\\tag{12}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b18", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b18", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.511, 0.217, 0.924, 0.248]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>where 0 represents the zero matrix, and I represents the unit matrix of the corresponding dimensions.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、0は零行列を、Iは対応する次元の単位行列を表す。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b19", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b19", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.51, 0.248, 0.925, 0.34]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>To design a linear controller, the non-linear equation of motion must first be linearized. It is common to approximate around the nominal operating point <span class=\"math inline\">\\((\\theta_{n},u_{n})\\)<\/span> by the first terms of the Taylor series <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-3\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-3\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Franklin et al., 2002<\/a>)<\/span>. The resulting equation of motion represented by appropriate state vector and state space matrices is as follow:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>線形コントローラを設計するには、まず非線形運動方程式を線形化する必要がある。公称動作点<span class=\"math inline\">\\((\\theta_{n},u_{n})\\)<\/span>の近傍において、テイラー級数<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-3\">Franklin et al.,\n2002<\/a>の初項を用いて近似するのが一般的である。適切な状態ベクトルおよび状態空間行列で表現される、得られる運動方程式は以下の通りである：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b20", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b20", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.513, 0.35, 0.922, 0.367]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_21.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\boldsymbol {\\Delta} \\dot {\\boldsymbol {\\theta}} (t) = \\mathbf {A} \\Delta \\boldsymbol {\\theta} (t) + \\mathbf {B} \\Delta u (t).\n\\tag{13}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "sec-p3-b21", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b21", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.511, 0.385, 0.802, 0.401]}], "html": "<h2 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p3-b21\">3 Stabilization control of the system<\/h2>", "translation_html": "\n<p>３ システムの安定化制御<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b22", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b22", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.51, 0.414, 0.924, 0.478]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>In this section, attention is paid to the possibilities of stabilizing the double-inverted pendulum. The LQR and feedback linearization as the theoretical basis for the following system of the swing-up search have achieved detailed description.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本節では、二重倒立振り子の安定化の可能性について考察する。スイングアップ探索の以下の系における理論的基盤として、LQRおよびフィードバック線形化について詳細な記述を行う。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p3-b23", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b23", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.511, 0.493, 0.785, 0.51]}], "html": "<h3 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p3-b23\">3.1 Linear quadratic regulator (LQR)<\/h3>", "translation_html": "\n<p>3.1 線形二次レギュレータ (LQR)<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b24", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b24", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.51, 0.517, 0.924, 0.595]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>The objective of this method is to design the optimal control of a linear system given the magnitude of the active intervention u and the deviation of the states x from the zero (desired) value in time. Practically, the objective is to minimize the cost function J , which is given by<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本手法の目的は、能動的介入 u の大きさと、時間経過に伴う状態 x\nのゼロ（目標）値からの偏差が与えられたとき、線形システムの最適制御を設計することである。実用上は、次式で与えられるコスト関数\nJ を最小化することが目的となる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b25", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b25", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.511, 0.604, 0.922, 0.656]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_26.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nJ = \\int_ {0} ^ {T} \\left(\\boldsymbol {x} ^ {T} (t) \\mathbf {Q} _ {\\mathrm{c}} \\boldsymbol {x} (t) + u ^ {T} (t) \\mathbf {R} _ {\\mathrm{c}} u (t)\\right) \\mathrm{d} t.\n\\tag{14}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b26", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b26", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.511, 0.665, 0.854, 0.681]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>For the state feedback law, we have the following:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>州のフィードバック法については、以下の通りです。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p3-b27", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b27", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.511, 0.693, 0.922, 0.709]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_2_equation_28.jpg\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nu (t) = - K _ {\\mathrm{c}} \\boldsymbol {x} (t).\n\\tag{15}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p3-b28", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p3-b28", "page": 3, "bbox": [0.51, 0.72, 0.925, 0.92]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"3\">\n<p>For discrete systems, the integral in Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-6\">6<\/a>) is replaced by the summation. The matrices <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{c}\\)<\/span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{c}\\)<\/span> correspond to the weights of the states and inputs, respectively <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-3\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-3\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Franklin et al., 2002<\/a>)<\/span>. <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\boldsymbol{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span> is the control matrix that can be subsequently used for stabilization and is given by the solution of the associated Riccati equation. LQR is a widely used method, and there is a wealth of documentation on it. Implementation-wise, the simplest modification of LQR for non-linear systems is the state-dependent Riccati equation (SDRE). The principle of the method is to linearize the model around the current state for each time instant and then compute the optimal control matrix. However, this method places greater demands on computational power.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>離散系では、式(<a href=\"#eq-6\">6<\/a>)の積分は総和に置き換えられる。行列<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{c}\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{c}\\)<\/span>は、それぞれ状態と入力の重み<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-3\">Franklin et al., 2002<\/a>に対応する。<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\boldsymbol{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span>はその後安定化に利用可能な制御行列であり、対応するリカッチ方程式の解によって与えられる。LQRは広く用いられている手法であり、これに関する文献が豊富に存在する。実装面では、非線形系に対するLQRの最も単純な修正形は、状態依存リカッチ方程式（SDRE）である。この手法の原理は、各時刻において現在の状態を中心にモデルを線形化し、最適制御行列を計算することにある。ただし、この手法は計算能力への要求がより高くなる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p4-b3", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b3", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.08, 0.322, 0.096]}], "html": "<h3 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p4-b3\">3.2 Feedback linearization (FBL)<\/h3>", "translation_html": "\n<p>3.2 フィードバック線形化 (FBL)<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b4", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b4", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.072, 0.104, 0.486, 0.181]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>In contrast to the usual linear function approximation, the method used does not neglect the non-linear terms and works even outside the vicinity of the working point. There are two principles utilized in combination in this work’s input state and input–output linearization.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>従来の線形関数近似とは異なり、本手法では非線形項を無視せず、作用点の近傍外においても有効に機能する。本研究の入力状態および入力－出力線形化においては、2つの原理を組み合わせて用いている。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b5", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.181, 0.486, 0.228]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>The necessary algebraic operations are generally not trivial. For the sake of scope, the system is restricted to the single input, single output (SISO) described by the following:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>必要な代数演算は一般に自明ではない。範囲を限定するため、本システムは以下で記述される単一入力・単一出力（SISO）に限定する。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b6", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b6", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.072, 0.234, 0.484, 0.308]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_6.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\dot {\\boldsymbol {x}} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} \\dot {x} _ {1} \\\\ \\ddots \\\\ \\dot {x} _ {n - 1} \\\\ \\dot {x} _ {n} \\end{array} \\right] = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} x _ {2} \\\\ \\ddots \\\\ x _ {n} \\\\ f (\\boldsymbol {x}) + g (\\boldsymbol {x}) u \\end{array} \\right].\n\\tag{16}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b7", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b7", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.072, 0.315, 0.485, 0.346]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>The input state linearization consists of finding a suitable transformation of the states T and input u such that<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>入力状態線形化とは、状態 T と入力 u\nの適切な変換を求め、次を満たすようにすることである。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b8", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b8", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.356, 0.484, 0.371]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_8.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\boldsymbol {z} = \\boldsymbol {T} (\\boldsymbol {x}), u = u (\\boldsymbol {x}, v).\n\\tag{17}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b9", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b9", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.381, 0.443, 0.397]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>The role of regulation is transferred to system control:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>規制の役割はシステム制御へと移行する：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b10", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b10", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.407, 0.484, 0.422]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_10.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\dot {z} = \\mathbf {A _ {c}} x + \\mathbf {B _ {c}} v.\n\\tag{18}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b11", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b11", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.072, 0.432, 0.486, 0.478]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>The linearization conditions, detailed description, and examples are exhaustively explained in <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-5\">Hedrick and Girard (<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">2010<\/a>)<\/span> and <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-4\">Graichen et al. (<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-4\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">2007<\/a>)<\/span>.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>線形化条件、詳細な説明、および例については、<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>および<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-4\">2007<\/a>で網羅的に解説されている。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b12", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b12", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.478, 0.486, 0.51]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>We assume that the outputs of the considered system y are given by the following function:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>検討対象とするシステムyの出力が、以下の関数で与えられるものとする：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b13", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b13", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.074, 0.518, 0.484, 0.534]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_13.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\ny = h (x).\n\\tag{19}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b14", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b14", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.544, 0.486, 0.606]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>The principle of the input–output linearization is to find the direct dependence of the outputs on the input by successively deriving the function h with regard to time until the following dependence appears:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>入出力線形化の原理は、次のような依存関係が現れるまで関数 h\nを時間に関して逐次的に導出することで、出力の入力に対する直接的な依存関係を求めることにある：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b15", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b15", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.614, 0.483, 0.666]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_15.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{c} \\mathbf {y} ^ {(1)} = \\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {h}}{\\partial \\boldsymbol {x}} \\frac {\\mathrm{d} x}{\\mathrm{d} t} = \\frac {\\partial \\boldsymbol {h}}{\\partial x} \\big [ f (\\boldsymbol {x}) + g (\\boldsymbol {x}) u \\big ] = L _ {\\mathrm{f}} (h) \\\\ + L _ {\\mathrm{g}} (\\boldsymbol {h}) u, \\mathbf {y} ^ {(2)} = L _ {\\mathrm{f}} ^ {2} (\\boldsymbol {h}) + L _ {\\mathrm{g}} (L _ {\\mathrm{f}} (\\boldsymbol {h})) u, \\end{array}\n\\tag{20}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b16", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b16", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.675, 0.485, 0.721]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>and so on until, for the kth derivative, the input term is non-zero <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-1\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-1\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Aguiar, 2011<\/a>)<\/span>. The prescription of the new input u is given by<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>というように、k階導関数において入力項は非ゼロとなる <a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-1\">Aguiar, 2011<\/a>。新たな入力 u\nの処方は次のように与えられる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b17", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b17", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.729, 0.484, 0.77]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_17.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nu = \\frac {1}{L _ {\\mathrm{g}} \\left(L _ {\\mathrm{f}} ^ {k - 1} (\\boldsymbol {h})\\right)} \\left(- L _ {\\mathrm{f}} ^ {k} (\\boldsymbol {h}) + v\\right),\n\\tag{21}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b18", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b18", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.072, 0.778, 0.486, 0.841]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>where v is equal to <span class=\"math inline\">\\(y(k)\\)<\/span> . The transformed systems prescribed by Eqs. (22, 23) are already completely linear – they can therefore be controlled by the linear method (LQR, array placement).<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで v は <span class=\"math inline\">\\(y(k)\\)<\/span>\nに等しい。式(22,\n23)で規定される変換後のシステムはすでに完全に線形であるため、線形法（LQR、アレイ配置）によって制御可能である。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b19", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b19", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.073, 0.847, 0.484, 0.921]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_19.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\dot {\\boldsymbol {z}} = \\left( \\begin{array}{c} y ^ {(1)} \\\\ \\ddots \\\\ y ^ {(k - 1)} \\\\ y ^ {(k)} \\end{array} \\right) = \\mathbf {A} _ {\\mathrm{c}} \\boldsymbol {z} + \\mathbf {B} _ {\\mathrm{c}} v\n\\tag{22}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b21", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b21", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.511, 0.262, 0.922, 0.403]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_3_equation_22.jpg\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{l} \\mathbf {A} _ {\\mathrm{c}} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c c c c c c} 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; \\ddots &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; \\ddots \\\\ \\ddots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\ddots \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\ddots &amp; 0 &amp; 1 \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\ddots &amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\end{array} \\right], \\mathbf {B} _ {\\mathrm{c}} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\ddots \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{array} \\right], \\\\ v = - K _ {\\mathrm{c}} z \\end{array}\n\\tag{23}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p4-b22", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b22", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.51, 0.413, 0.925, 0.505]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>A schematic of the closed-loop control is shown in Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-3\">3<\/a>. For systems with n inputs and m outputs (MIMO), where <span class=\"math inline\">\\(n = m\\)<\/span> the procedure is more complicated (we refer to static input– output decoupling), but the basic principles remain the same <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-5 paper-ref-7\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>; <a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-7\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Henson and Seborg, 1997<\/a>)<\/span> and lead to time-invariant feedback control.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>閉ループ制御の概略図を図<a href=\"#fig-3\">3<\/a>に示す。n個の入力とm個の出力を持つシステム（MIMO）では、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(n = m\\)<\/span>\n手順はより複雑になるが（静的な入出力デカップリングと呼ぶ）、基本原理は同一であり<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>; <a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-7\">Henson and Seborg,\n1997<\/a>、時不変のフィードバック制御につながる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b23", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b23", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.509, 0.505, 0.926, 0.705]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>Also, A Kalman filter, which is a very useful tool that extracts the best possible estimate of all the states of the system (even if not all of them are measured) from imperfect knowledge of the model and inaccurate measurements <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-11\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-11\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Nise, 2020<\/a>)<\/span>, is used in this work. This is a stochastic observer – it assumes that the quantities are random with a Gaussian distribution and works with their mean and variance (uncertainty). Tuning of the algorithm consists of an appropriate choice of the matrices <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathbf{Q}_{0}\\)<\/span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\left|R_{0}\\right|\\)<\/span> which introduce the co-variance of process and measurement noise into the calculation. At each stage, the state estimation and covariance matrix <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\left|\\mathbf{P}_{0}\\right|\\)<\/span> are adjusted, which carries information about the uncertainty of the states and their correlation with each other.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>また、本研究では、モデルに関する不完全な知見や不正確な測定値（<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-11\">Nise,\n2020<\/a>）から、システムのすべての状態（すべてが測定されているわけではない場合でも）の可能な限り最適な推定値を抽出する非常に有用なツールであるカルマンフィルタを採用している。これは確率的オブザーバであり、各量がガウス分布に従うランダムな値であると仮定し、その平均と分散（不確かさ）を用いて動作する。アルゴリズムのチューニングは、プロセスノイズと測定ノイズの共分散を計算に組み込むための、行列<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathbf{Q}_{0}\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\left|R_{0}\\right|\\)<\/span>の適切な選択によって行われる。各段階において、状態推定および共分散行列<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\left|\\mathbf{P}_{0}\\right|\\)<\/span>が調整され、これにより状態の不確かさとそれら相互の相関に関する情報が保持される。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p4-b24", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b24", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.511, 0.722, 0.674, 0.738]}], "html": "<h2 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p4-b24\">4 Swing-up control<\/h2>", "translation_html": "\n<p>4 スイングアップ制御<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p4-b25", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p4-b25", "page": 4, "bbox": [0.509, 0.75, 0.926, 0.92]}, {"id": "p5-b3", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.071, 0.253, 0.487, 0.331]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"4\">\n<p>The key to planning a swing-up is finding a suitable trajectory for the carriage and pendulums so that the positions and velocities of the carriage and pendulums are zero when the swing-up is complete. However, whatever the method of obtaining the swing-up trajectory (or the necessary input for swing-up), in terms of structure, it is possible to divide the control into forward or backward. Feedforward control can only be used if the behavior of the double-inverted pendulum is well known. A previously calculated input is applied to the system, and a certain output is expected. However, the double-inverse pendulum is extremely sensitive to initial conditions. Even a small deviation from the calculated trajectory can cause a failed swing-up. A possible solution is to add feedback control. If we denote by <span class=\"math inline\">\\(u_{f}\\)<\/span> the input given by as the forward control and that given by <span class=\"math inline\">\\(u_{b}\\)<\/span> as the backward control, then the resultant is given by their sum (Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-4\">4<\/a>).<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>スイングアップを計画する際の鍵は、スイングアップ完了時にキャリッジと振り子の位置および速度がゼロとなるよう、両者に適した軌道を見出すことにある。しかし、スイングアップ軌道（あるいはスイングアップに必要な入力）の取得方法にかかわらず、構造上の観点からは、制御を前進または後退に分けることが可能である。フィードフォワード制御は、二重反転振り子の挙動が十分に解明されている場合にのみ使用できる。あらかじめ計算された入力をシステムに適用し、特定の出力を期待する。しかし、二重反転振り子は初期条件に対して極めて敏感である。計算された軌道からわずかでも逸脱すると、スイングアップに失敗することがある。考えられる解決策は、フィードバック制御を追加することである。<span class=\"math inline\">\\(u_{f}\\)<\/span>を前進制御、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(u_{b}\\)<\/span>を後退制御とする入力とすると、合成結果はそれらの和で与えられる（図<a href=\"#fig-4\">4<\/a>）。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p5-b4", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b4", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.073, 0.347, 0.485, 0.364]}], "html": "<h3 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p5-b4\">4.1 Boundary value problem (BVP) with free parameters<\/h3>", "translation_html": "\n<p>4.1 自由パラメータを持つ境界値問題 (BVP)<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b5", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.072, 0.371, 0.487, 0.433]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>Finding a trajectory for the swing-up function is a case of the boundary value problem. The equation of motion (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-1\">1<\/a>) is a system of ordinary differential equations (ODEs), and the boundary conditions are as follows:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>スイングアップ関数の軌道を求める問題は、境界値問題である。運動方程式（<a href=\"#eq-1\">1<\/a>）は常微分方程式系（ODE）であり、境界条件は以下の通りである。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b6", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b6", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.073, 0.442, 0.484, 0.482]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_7.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{c} \\boldsymbol {\\theta} _ {0} (t = 0) = [ 0, \\pi , \\pi , 0, 0, 0 ] ^ {T}, \\boldsymbol {\\theta} _ {T} (t = T) \\\\ = [ 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 ] ^ {T}, \\end{array}\n\\tag{24}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b7", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b7", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.072, 0.493, 0.487, 0.587]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>where t is the time, and T is the duration of the swing. For the 6 equations and 12 conditions, the associated boundary value problem is overdetermined. In order to solve it, <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-12\">Qian et al. (<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-12\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">2011<\/a>)<\/span> propose defining the cart trajectory <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Y(t)\\)<\/span> by the cosine series (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-13\">13<\/a>) and thus adding the necessary number of free <span class=\"math inline\">\\(p = \\left[p_{1}  p_{2}  p_{3}  p_{4}\\right]\\)<\/span> to the equation of motion.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、tは時間、Tはスイングの持続時間である。6つの方程式と12個の条件に対し、対応する境界値問題は過決定となっている。これを解くため、<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-12\">2011<\/a>ではカートの軌道<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Y(t)\\)<\/span>を余弦級数（<a href=\"#eq-13\">13<\/a>）で定義し、運動方程式に必要な数の自由変数<span class=\"math inline\">\\(p =\n\\left[p_{1}  p_{2}  p_{3}  p_{4}\\right]\\)<\/span>を加える手法を提案している。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b8", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b8", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.073, 0.597, 0.484, 0.637]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_9.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nY (t, p) = a _ {0} + a _ {1} \\cos \\left(\\frac {\\pi t}{T}\\right) + \\sum_ {i = 2} ^ {5} p _ {i - 1} \\cos \\left(\\frac {i \\pi t}{T}\\right)\n\\tag{25}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b9", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b9", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.072, 0.645, 0.487, 0.753]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>The terms <span class=\"math inline\">\\(a_0 = -(p_1 + p_3)\\)<\/span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(a_1 = -(p_2 + p_4)\\)<\/span> are obtained by setting <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Y(0,p)=Y(T,p)=0\\)<\/span> , which appears by deriving Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-13\">13<\/a>) by time. The boundary value problem can be solved by a suitable numerical method. If the deviation of the actual state values from the nominal trajectory <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\boldsymbol{\\theta}^{*}\\)<\/span> and input <span class=\"math inline\">\\(u^{*}\\)<\/span> is sufficiently small, the system can be described by a linear time-dependent state equation <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-14\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-14\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Zhong and Rock, 2001<\/a>)<\/span>:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>項<span class=\"math inline\">\\(a_0 = -(p_1 + p_3)\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(a_1 = -(p_2 + p_4)\\)<\/span>は、式(<a href=\"#eq-13\">13<\/a>)を時間発展させることで得られる<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Y(0,p)=Y(T,p)=0\\)<\/span>を設定することで導出される。境界値問題は、適切な数値解法によって解くことができる。実際の状態値と公称軌道<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\boldsymbol{\\theta}^{*}\\)<\/span>および入力<span class=\"math inline\">\\(u^{*}\\)<\/span>との偏差が十分に小さい場合、系は線形時間依存状態方程式<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-14\">Zhong and Rock, 2001<\/a>で記述できる：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b10", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b10", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.074, 0.761, 0.484, 0.779]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_11.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\Delta \\dot {\\boldsymbol {\\theta}} (t) = \\mathbf {A} (t) \\Delta \\boldsymbol {\\theta} (t) + \\mathbf {B} (t) \\Delta u (t),\n\\tag{26}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b11", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b11", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.072, 0.789, 0.486, 0.852]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>where the matrices A and B are given by the linearization of Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-12\">12<\/a>) (see “Feedback linearization” section) along the nominal trajectory and input. And for such a system, we design a linear controller at each time instant:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、行列AおよびBは、公称軌道および入力に沿った式(<a href=\"#eq-12\">12<\/a>)の線形化（「フィードバック線形化」節参照）によって与えられる。このようなシステムに対し、各時刻において線形制御器を設計する：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b12", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b12", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.074, 0.861, 0.484, 0.878]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_13.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\Delta u (t) = - \\boldsymbol {K} _ {\\mathrm{c}} (t) \\Delta \\theta (t) = - \\boldsymbol {K} _ {\\mathrm{c}} (t) (\\boldsymbol {\\theta} (t) - \\boldsymbol {\\theta} ^ {*} (t)),\n\\tag{27}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b13", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b13", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.072, 0.888, 0.486, 0.919]}, {"id": "p5-b14", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.51, 0.081, 0.924, 0.127]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>where the control matrix K is computed forward. Its calculation therefore does not burden the processor on which the swing-up and subsequent stabilization program runs. The resulting forward and backward control actions are given by the following:<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、制御行列Kは順方向に算出される。したがって、その計算が、スイングアップおよびその後の安定化プログラムが実行されるプロセッサに負荷をかけることはない。結果として得られる順方向および逆方向の制御動作は、以下のように与えられる：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b15", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b15", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.51, 0.138, 0.922, 0.157]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_16.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nu (t) = u _ {\\mathrm{a}} (t) + \\boldsymbol {K} _ {\\mathrm{c}} (t) \\left(\\boldsymbol {\\theta} ^ {*} (t) - \\boldsymbol {\\theta} (t)\\right).\n\\tag{28}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "sec-p5-b16", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b16", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.511, 0.173, 0.811, 0.189]}], "html": "<h3 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p5-b16\">4.2 Partial linearization and feedforward<\/h3>", "translation_html": "\n<p>4.2 部分的線形化とフィードフォワード<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b17", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b17", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.509, 0.198, 0.924, 0.274]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>By studying the natural motion of a system (without control), some useful knowledge can be gained. In order to calculate a suitable elevation trajectory, the natural frequencies of the system must be found. This is based on the findings of the feedback linearization (FBL).<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>システムの自然な運動（制御なし）を解析することで、いくつかの有用な知見を得ることができる。適切な仰角軌道を算出するには、システムの固有振動数を求める必要がある。これはフィードバック線形化（FBL）の知見に基づいている。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b18", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b18", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.509, 0.274, 0.925, 0.367]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>For the sake of partial linearization, the generalized coordinates of the double-inverse pendulum and the variable vector q are divided into two parts; <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q}_{x}\\)<\/span> denotes the controlled part (the carriage), and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q}_{\\theta}\\)<\/span> denotes the rest with zero dynamics (the pendulum). With the proposed decomposition, Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-5\">5<\/a>) is decomposed into the following:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>部分的な線形化のため、二重逆振り子と変数ベクトルqの一般化座標を2つの部分に分割する。<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q}_{x}\\)<\/span>は制御部分（台車）を、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q}_{\\theta}\\)<\/span>はダイナミクスがゼロの残りの部分（振り子）を表す。提案する分解により、式(<a href=\"#eq-5\">5<\/a>)は以下のように分解される：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b19", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b19", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.511, 0.378, 0.922, 0.396]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_20.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\mathbf {M} _ {x x} \\ddot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {x} + \\mathbf {M} _ {x \\theta} \\ddot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {\\theta} + \\mathbf {B} _ {x x} \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {\\mathrm{X}} + \\mathbf {B} _ {x \\theta} \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {\\theta} = u,\n\\tag{29}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b20", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b20", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.511, 0.434, 0.922, 0.452]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_21.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\mathbf {M} _ {\\theta x} \\ddot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {x} + \\mathbf {M} _ {\\theta \\theta} \\ddot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {\\theta} + \\mathbf {B} _ {\\theta \\theta} \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {\\theta} + \\mathbf {K} _ {\\theta} = 0,\n\\tag{30}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b21", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b21", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.511, 0.463, 0.778, 0.479]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>and the matrices M, B, and K become<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>そして行列 M, B, K は<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b22", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b22", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.511, 0.489, 0.826, 0.595]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_23.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\left| \\begin{array}{l} \\mathbf {M} (q) = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c c} \\mathbf {M} _ {x x} (1, 1) &amp; \\mathbf {M} _ {x \\theta} (1, 2) \\\\ \\mathbf {M} _ {\\theta x} (2, 1) &amp; \\mathbf {M} _ {\\theta \\theta} (2, 2) \\end{array} \\right], \\mathbf {B} (\\boldsymbol {q}, \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}}) \\\\ = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c c} \\mathbf {B} _ {x x} (1, 1) &amp; \\mathbf {B} _ {x \\theta} (1, 2) \\\\ \\mathbf {0} (2, 1) &amp; \\mathbf {B} _ {\\theta \\theta} (2, 2) \\end{array} \\right], \\mathbf {K} (\\boldsymbol {q}, \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}}) \\\\ = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} 0 \\\\ \\mathbf {K} _ {\\theta} (2, 1) \\end{array} \\right], \\end{array} \\right|\n\\]<\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b23", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b23", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.51, 0.604, 0.924, 0.698]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>where 0 represents the zero vector, and the numbers in parentheses indicate the dimension of the matrix – so, for example, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathbf{M}_{x\\theta} = [d_{2}\\cos \\theta_{1} d_{3}\\cos \\theta_{2}]\\)<\/span> . From Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-30\">30<\/a>), <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\left|\\ddot{\\boldsymbol{q}}_{\\theta}\\right|\\)<\/span> is expressed and substituted into Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-29\">29<\/a>). If the output of the system is <span class=\"math inline\">\\(y = q_{x}\\)<\/span> , then the feedback linearization of the obtained equation gives the following:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、0は零ベクトルを表し、括弧内の数値は行列の次元を示す。例えば、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathbf{M}_{x\\theta} = [d_{2}\\cos \\theta_{1}\nd_{3}\\cos \\theta_{2}]\\)<\/span> となる。式(<a href=\"#eq-30\">30<\/a>)から<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\left|\\ddot{\\boldsymbol{q}}_{\\theta}\\right|\\)<\/span>を表し、これを式(<a href=\"#eq-29\">29<\/a>)に代入する。システムの出力が<span class=\"math inline\">\\(y =\nq_{x}\\)<\/span>である場合、得られた方程式をフィードバック線形化すると以下のようになる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b24", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b24", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.511, 0.709, 0.922, 0.766]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_4_equation_25.jpg\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\begin{array}{l} \\ddot {y} = \\ddot {q} _ {x} = v, \\\\ u = \\mathbf {B} _ {x x} \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {x} + (\\mathbf {B} _ {x \\theta} + \\mathbf {W B} _ {\\theta \\theta}) \\dot {\\boldsymbol {q}} _ {\\theta} + \\mathbf {W K} _ {\\theta} \\\\ \\quad + (\\mathbf {W M} _ {\\theta x} + \\mathbf {M} _ {x x}) v, \\end{array}\n\\tag{31}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p5-b25", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b25", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.891, 0.751, 0.922, 0.765]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<ol start=\"32\" type=\"1\">\n<li><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<ol start=\"32\" type=\"1\">\n<li><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b26", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b26", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.511, 0.78, 0.849, 0.797]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>where, to simplify the notation, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathbf{W} = -\\mathbf{M}_{x\\theta}\\mathbf{M}_{\\theta \\theta}^{-1}\\)<\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ここで、表記を簡略化するため、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mathbf{W}\n= -\\mathbf{M}_{x\\theta}\\mathbf{M}_{\\theta \\theta}^{-1}\\)<\/span><\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p5-b27", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p5-b27", "page": 5, "bbox": [0.509, 0.797, 0.925, 0.92]}, {"id": "p6-b3", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.073, 0.241, 0.486, 0.287]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"5\">\n<p>The principle further consists of finding an input v for which the boundary conditions in Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-24\">24<\/a>) hold. In general, it is given by the sum of two parts. The first makes the cart move a certain distance from the initial state at time T . However, since the end position of the cart is supposed to be identical to the initial position, i.e., <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_0(0) = \\theta_0(T) = 0\\)<\/span> , the mentioned component will be zero for this case. The second component does not change the final position of the cart, but due to the entanglement via zero dynamics, it will cause the pendulums to swing. It is proposed in the following form <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-5\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>)<\/span>:<\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本原理はさらに、式(<a href=\"#eq-24\">24<\/a>)の境界条件が成立する入力vを求めることで構成される。一般に、これは2つの成分の和として与えられる。第1の成分は、時刻Tにおいて台車を初期状態から一定の距離だけ移動させる。しかし、台車の最終位置は初期位置、すなわち<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_0(0) = \\theta_0(T) =\n0\\)<\/span>と同一であるはずであるため、この場合、当該成分はゼロとなる。第2の成分は台車の最終位置を変化させないが、ゼロダイナミクスによるもつれのため、振り子を揺動させる。これは以下の形式<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-5\">Hedrick and Girard, 2010<\/a>で提案される：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p6-b4", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b4", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.074, 0.294, 0.484, 0.325]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_5_equation_5.jpg\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\nv = \\sum_ {i} A _ {i} \\sin (2 \\pi f _ {i} t + \\varphi_ {i}).\n\\tag{33}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p6-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b5", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.073, 0.335, 0.485, 0.367]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p>The amplitudes <span class=\"math inline\">\\(A_{i}\\)<\/span> are relative to the change in the potential energy of the system:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>振幅 <span class=\"math inline\">\\(A_{i}\\)<\/span>\nは、系のポテンシャルエネルギーの変化に対する相対値である：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p6-b6", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b6", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.074, 0.378, 0.484, 0.395]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_5_equation_7.jpg\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n\\Delta E _ {p} = m _ {1} l _ {1} g + m _ {2} (L _ {1} + l _ {2}) g.\n\\tag{34}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "p6-b7", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b7", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.072, 0.405, 0.486, 0.482]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p>However, the exact numbers, as well as the phase shifts <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\varphi_{i}\\)<\/span> are the result of an optimization process to obtain boundary conditions for the <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q}_{\\theta}\\)<\/span> coordinates as well. If there are natural numbers <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\boldsymbol{K}_{i}\\)<\/span> , then the following holds <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"paper-ref-10\">(<a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-10\" role=\"doc-biblioref\">Neusser and Valášek, 2013<\/a>)<\/span>:<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>ただし、正確な数値および位相シフト <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\varphi_{i}\\)<\/span> は、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\pmb{q}_{\\theta}\\)<\/span>\n座標についても境界条件を得るための最適化プロセスの結果である。自然数\n<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\boldsymbol{K}_{i}\\)<\/span>\nが存在する場合、以下が成り立つ <a href=\"#ref-paper-ref-10\">Neusser and\nValášek, 2013<\/a>：<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p6-b8", "kind": "equation", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b8", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.073, 0.493, 0.484, 0.509]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block\" data-equation-image=\"images/page_5_equation_9.jpg\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p><span><span class=\"math display\">\\[\n2 \\pi \\boldsymbol {f} _ {i} T = 2 \\pi \\boldsymbol {K} _ {i}.\n\\tag{35}\\]<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": null}, {"id": "sec-p6-b9", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b9", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.073, 0.527, 0.196, 0.543]}], "html": "<h2 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p6-b9\">5 Simulations<\/h2>", "translation_html": "\n<p>5 シミュレーション<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p6-b10", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b10", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.071, 0.555, 0.487, 0.785]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p>The calculations of the linearized model and the gains of the controller and observer are shown in Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-5\">5<\/a>. In order to avoid the errors as much as possible, after deriving Eq. (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-5\">5<\/a>), all further modifications were performed using the Symbolic Math Toolbox in MATLAB. In this way, the equation of motion (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-12\">12<\/a>) and its linearized form in the form of state space matrices A and B were obtained. These are complex relations with a considerable number of terms. The system was further simulated in Simulink environment with an ode4 (Runge–Kutta) solver with a constant time step of 0.001 s. The verification of the equation of motion (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-12\">12<\/a>) was successful. It faithfully describes the model under consideration. This is one of the basic prerequisites for the design of a successful control algorithm. The parameters used in the simulation are shown in Table <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#tbl-1\">1<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>線形化モデルの計算結果および制御器とオブザーバのゲインを図<a href=\"#fig-5\">5<\/a>に示す。誤差を可能な限り回避するため、式(<a href=\"#eq-5\">5<\/a>)を導出した後、以降のすべての修正はMATLABのSymbolic\nMath Toolboxを用いて行った。これにより、運動方程式(<a href=\"#eq-12\">12<\/a>)および状態空間行列AおよびBの形式によるその線形化形が得られた。これらは項数が非常に多い複雑な関係式である。さらに、本システムをSimulink環境において、定数時間ステップ0.001\nsのODE4（ルンゲ＝クッタ）ソルバーを用いてシミュレーションした。運動方程式(<a href=\"#eq-12\">12<\/a>)の検証は成功し、検討対象のモデルを忠実に記述している。これは、成功する制御アルゴリズムを設計するための基本的な前提条件の一つである。シミュレーションに使用したパラメータを表<a href=\"#tbl-1\">1<\/a>に示す。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p6-b11", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b11", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.073, 0.802, 0.333, 0.819]}], "html": "<h3 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p6-b11\">5.1 Stabilization control simulation<\/h3>", "translation_html": "\n<p>5.1 安定化制御シミュレーション<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p6-b12", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b12", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.072, 0.826, 0.487, 0.92]}, {"id": "p6-b14", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.509, 0.335, 0.926, 0.627]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p>In Sect. 3.1 in this article, the method of obtaining the linear equations of the system described by the matrices A and B was explained. The optimal control multipliers K were calculated based on the model and the given weight matrices <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span> . An extended Kalman filter was used as an observer to perform the correction based on the measurement of the carriage position and the pendulum rotation. The <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{c}\\)<\/span> for the LQR controller and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{Kal}}\\)<\/span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{\\mathrm{Kal}}\\)<\/span> for the Kalman filter are chosen as follows: <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{c}} = \\mathrm{diag}[10350350000],R_{\\mathrm{c}} =\\)<\/span> 1 , <span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{Kal}} = \\mathrm{diag}[0.1 \\quad 0.03 \\quad 0.03 \\quad 0.15 \\quad 0.4 \\quad 0.4]\\)<\/span> , and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{\\mathrm{Kal}} = \\mathrm{diag}[0.3\\quad 0.7\\quad 0.7]\\)<\/span> . Sensor noise was simulated at this stage by random numbers with a Gaussian distribution around zero mean. Nevertheless, the stabilization task was very easy compared to the subsequent tuning on the real system. The main objective of the simulation was to verify the correctness of the programming and the functionality of the algorithm. Figure <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-6\">6<\/a> shows the stabilization waveform for initial conditions <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_0 = 0.2\\mathrm{m},\\theta_1 = 10^\\circ\\)<\/span> , and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_{2} = -10^{\\circ}\\)<\/span> . The desired carriage position is indicated in red in the figure. This is because the positioning of the carriage is relatively easy to achieve since the stability of the system does not depend on <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_{0}\\)<\/span> as the only one of the states. The control law was given as <span class=\"math inline\">\\(u(t) = Nr(t) - \\mathbf{K}x(t);r(t)\\)<\/span> is the desired cart position, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(N=-\\mathbf{B}^{-1}(\\mathbf{A}-\\mathbf{B}\\mathbf{K})\\mathbf{C}^{T}\\)<\/span> , and for this case <span class=\"math inline\">\\(C = [0.100000]\\)<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本論文の第3.1節では、行列AおよびBで記述される系の線形方程式の導出方法について説明した。最適制御乗数Kは、モデルおよび与えられた重み行列<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span>に基づいて算出した。台車位置と振り子回転の計測値に基づく補正を行うため、オブザーバとして拡張カルマンフィルタを用いた。LQRコントローラ用の<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{c}\\)<\/span>、ならびにカルマンフィルタ用の<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{Kal}}\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{\\mathrm{Kal}}\\)<\/span>は、それぞれ次のように選定した：<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{c}} =\n\\mathrm{diag}[10350350000],R_{\\mathrm{c}} =\\)<\/span> 1、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(Q_{\\mathrm{Kal}} = \\mathrm{diag}[0.1 \\quad 0.03\n\\quad 0.03 \\quad 0.15 \\quad 0.4 \\quad 0.4]\\)<\/span>、および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(R_{\\mathrm{Kal}} = \\mathrm{diag}[0.3\\quad 0.7\\quad\n0.7]\\)<\/span>。この段階では、センサノイズを平均ゼロのガウス分布に従う乱数でシミュレートした。とはいえ、安定化処理は、その後の実システムにおけるチューニングに比べて非常に容易であった。シミュレーションの主な目的は、プログラミングの正確性とアルゴリズムの機能性を検証することであった。図<a href=\"#fig-6\">6<\/a>は、初期条件<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_0 =\n0.2\\mathrm{m},\\theta_1 = 10^\\circ\\)<\/span>および<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_{2} =\n-10^{\\circ}\\)<\/span>における安定化波形を示している。図中では、目標とする台車位置が赤色で示されている。これは、系の安定性が状態変数として<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\theta_{0}\\)<\/span>のみに依存しないため、台車の位置決めが比較的容易に達成できるからである。制御則は、目標台車位置を<span class=\"math inline\">\\(u(t) = Nr(t) - \\mathbf{K}x(t);r(t)\\)<\/span>、<span class=\"math inline\">\\(N=-\\mathbf{B}^{-1}(\\mathbf{A}-\\mathbf{B}\\mathbf{K})\\mathbf{C}^{T}\\)<\/span>とし、本ケースでは<span class=\"math inline\">\\(C = [0.100000]\\)<\/span>として設定した。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p6-b15", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b15", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.511, 0.649, 0.752, 0.665]}], "html": "<h3 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p6-b15\">5.2 Swing-up control simulation<\/h3>", "translation_html": "\n<p>5.2 スイングアップ制御シミュレーション<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p6-b16", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p6-b16", "page": 6, "bbox": [0.508, 0.675, 0.926, 0.92]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"6\">\n<p>In this section, the simulation results of swing-up trajectories and the subsequent application of forward and reverse control are addressed. The MATLAB numerical solver bvp4c was used to find suitable swing-up trajectories according to the method described in Sect. 4.1. For the double-pendulum model, where the input is the acceleration of the trolley, boundary conditions (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-24\">24<\/a>) were considered, except for defining the end position of the cart and its velocity, for which the boundary value is guaranteed by choosing the input as a cosine series (<a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#eq-13\">13<\/a>). A time-dependent linear controller was designed along the nominal swing-up trajectory (with a time step of 10 ms and subsequent linear interpolation between the calculated points). It turned out that, over a certain time interval, the control multiples undergo abrupt changes in magnitude and sign. Since the linear controller was derived from a double-pendulum model where the input is directly the ac-<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>本節では、スイングアップ軌道のシミュレーション結果と、それに続く正逆制御の適用について述べる。第4.1節で述べた手法に従い、MATLAB数値ソルバーbvp4cを用いて適切なスイングアップ軌道を求めた。トロリーの加速度を入力とする二重振り子モデルにおいて、台車の終端位置および速度の定義を除き、境界条件（<a href=\"#eq-24\">24<\/a>）を考慮した。なお、台車の終端位置および速度については、入力を余弦級数として設定することで境界値を保証した（<a href=\"#eq-13\">13<\/a>）。公称スイングアップ軌道に沿って、時間依存型線形制御器を設計した（時間ステップは10\nmsとし、計算点間には線形補間を適用した）。その結果、一定の時間間隔において、制御ゲインの大きさと符号が急激に変化することが判明した。この線形制御器は、入力が直接ac-となる二重振り子モデルから導出されたものである。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p7-b4", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p7-b4", "page": 7, "bbox": [0.073, 0.461, 0.487, 0.553]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"7\">\n<p>celeration of the carriage, its proposed intervention also has an acceleration dimension. Therefore, it has to be converted to a force based on the current states according to Eq. (32). In view of this and the fact that the system is often at the limit of drivability or loses it completely at these moments, it was decided to take the reverse steering out of action for a while.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>台車の加速に伴い、提案されている介入にも加速の要素が含まれる。したがって、式(32)に基づき、現在の状態に応じた力へと変換する必要がある。この点、およびシステムがこうした局面においてしばしば走行限界に達するか、あるいは完全に走行不能になるという事実に鑑み、リバースステアリングを一時的に停止させることとした。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p7-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p7-b5", "page": 7, "bbox": [0.072, 0.553, 0.487, 0.797]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"7\">\n<p>In Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-7\">7<\/a>, the swing-up state behavior is shown. It is clear that the control approach successfully followed the derived trajectory and moved the system from the downward to upward position in a short amount of time. All the states of the system are stable and follow the desired values. The actual and the estimated states of the system converge perfectly, which proves the effectiveness of the dynamic input– output decoupling approach. The abrupt disengagement and engagement of the reverse control caused a disproportionately large impulse response with the eventual consequence of loss of stability and a failed swing-up. Therefore, around the critical interval, the multiples <span class=\"math inline\">\\(K_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span> are linearly decreased or increased, as presented in Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-8\">8<\/a>. For the simulation, it is useful to set the duration of the linear region to 0.1 s. If the pendulum rotation approaches the inverse position during the swing-up, it is switched to LQG stabilization.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>図<a href=\"#fig-7\">7<\/a>に、スイングアップ状態の挙動を示す。制御手法が導出された軌道に忠実に従い、短時間でシステムを下方位置から上方位置へと移行させたことは明らかである。システムのすべての状態は安定しており、目標値に追従している。システムの実測状態と推定状態は完全に収束しており、これは動的入出力デカップリング手法の有効性を裏付けるものである。逆制御の急激な解除および再入力により、不釣り合いに大きなインパルス応答が生じ、結果として安定性の喪失とスイングアップの失敗に至った。したがって、臨界区間付近では、図<a href=\"#fig-8\">8<\/a>に示すように、複数の<span class=\"math inline\">\\(K_{\\mathrm{c}}\\)<\/span>が線形に減少または増加する。シミュレーションにおいては、線形領域の持続時間を0.1\nsに設定することが有用である。スイングアップ中に振り子の回転が逆位置に近づくと、LQG安定化に切り替わる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p7-b6", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p7-b6", "page": 7, "bbox": [0.072, 0.797, 0.487, 0.92]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"7\">\n<p>Trajectories with a duration of 1.85 s were selected for simulation purposes. The progress of such a swing-up is illustrated by the video sequence at the following link: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zr0fzmVc9Ao\">https://youtu.be/zr0fzmVc9Ao<\/a> (last access: 18 January 2024). In Fig. <a class=\"quarto-xref\" href=\"#fig-9\">9<\/a>, the process of swing-up control is illustrated by following the pendulums during the motion. The animation shows that the swing-up process effectively finished based on the designed controller.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>シミュレーション目的で、持続時間1.85秒の軌道を選定した。このようなスイングアップの過程は、以下のリンクの動画シーケンスで示されている：<a href=\"https://youtu.be/zr0fzmVc9Ao\">https://youtu.be/zr0fzmVc9Ao<\/a>（最終閲覧日：2024年1月18日）。図<a href=\"#fig-9\">9<\/a>では、動作中の振り子を追跡することで、スイングアップ制御の過程を示している。アニメーションからは、設計したコントローラに基づき、スイングアップの過程が効果的に完了したことがわかる。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "sec-p7-b10", "kind": "heading", "sources": [{"id": "p7-b10", "page": 7, "bbox": [0.511, 0.574, 0.639, 0.589]}], "html": "<h2 class=\"anchored\" data-anchor-id=\"sec-p7-b10\">6 Conclusions<\/h2>", "translation_html": "\n<p>6 結論<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p7-b11", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p7-b11", "page": 7, "bbox": [0.51, 0.602, 0.924, 0.693]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"7\">\n<p>A model of the double-inverted pendulum was obtained, including the assumption of all necessary parameters. Also, thanks to this, a robust and long-lasting stabilization of both pendulums in the inverted position was implemented. This is implemented by the LQR method. The system states are estimated by a non-linear extended Kalman filter.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>必要なすべてのパラメータを仮定した二重倒立振り子のモデルを構築した。これにより、倒立状態における両振り子の頑健かつ長期的な安定化を実現した。これはLQR法によって実装されている。システム状態は、非線形拡張カルマンフィルタによって推定される。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p7-b12", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p7-b12", "page": 7, "bbox": [0.509, 0.693, 0.926, 0.848]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"7\">\n<p>By solving the boundary value problem with the numerical proper solver, nominal trajectories for the swing-up function have been obtained. The required cart acceleration was implemented by a controller with 2 degrees of freedom – a forward PID control of the cart speed and a feedback LQR controller, whose controller gains were calculated off-line along the nominal trajectories and input. Fortunately, the planned swing-up was achieved despite the chaotic behavior of the real system. The algorithm proved its worth in simulation; a complete swing-up was still realized several times.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p>数値的適正ソルバーを用いて境界値問題を解くことで、スイングアップ関数の公称軌道を得た。必要な台車加速度は、2自由度のコントローラ――台車速度の順方向PID制御とフィードバックLQRコントローラ――によって実装され、そのコントローラゲインは公称軌道および入力に沿ってオフラインで算出した。幸いなことに、実システムのカオス的な挙動にもかかわらず、計画通りのスイングアップが実現した。本アルゴリズムはシミュレーションにおいてその有用性を実証し、完全なスイングアップが数回実現した。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p8-b2", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p8-b2", "page": 8, "bbox": [0.073, 0.082, 0.485, 0.125]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"8\">\n<p><strong>Data availability.<\/strong> The data that support the findings of this study are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p><strong>データの利用可能性。<\/strong>\n本研究の知見を裏付けるデータは、合理的な要請に基づき、責任著者から入手可能である。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p8-b3", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p8-b3", "page": 8, "bbox": [0.073, 0.154, 0.485, 0.211]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"8\">\n<p><strong>Author contributions.<\/strong> AMAJ conceived the idea and mathematical modeling. MTH was responsible the programming and finding the results. ASG Qanber was responsible for the proofreading and financial support.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p><strong>著者の貢献。<\/strong>\nAMAJが構想および数理モデリングを担当。MTHがプログラミングおよび結果の導出を担当。ASG\nQanberが校正および資金面での支援を担当。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p8-b4", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p8-b4", "page": 8, "bbox": [0.073, 0.24, 0.485, 0.269]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"8\">\n<p><strong>Competing interests.<\/strong> The contact author has declared that none of the authors has any competing interests.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p><strong>利益相反。<\/strong>\n責任著者は、著者のいずれにも利益相反がないことを申告しています。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p8-b5", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p8-b5", "page": 8, "bbox": [0.073, 0.298, 0.486, 0.383]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"8\">\n<p><strong>Disclaimer.<\/strong> Publisher’s note: Copernicus Publications remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims made in the text, published maps, institutional affiliations, or any other geographical representation in this paper. While Copernicus Publications makes every effort to include appropriate place names, the final responsibility lies with the authors.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p><strong>免責事項。<\/strong> 出版社注：Copernicus\nPublicationsは、本論文における管轄権の主張、掲載地図、所属機関、またはその他の地理的表示に関して、中立的な立場を維持します。Copernicus\nPublicationsは適切な地名を記載するよう最善を尽くしておりますが、最終的な責任は著者にあります。<\/p>\n"}, {"id": "p8-b6", "kind": "paragraph", "sources": [{"id": "p8-b6", "page": 8, "bbox": [0.073, 0.412, 0.485, 0.442]}], "html": "<div class=\"paper-block prose-block\" data-source-page=\"8\">\n<p><strong>Review statement.<\/strong> This paper was edited by Daniel Condurache and reviewed by Petr Chalupa and one anonymous referee.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>", "translation_html": "\n<p><strong>査読声明。<\/strong> 本論文はDaniel Conduracheが編集し、Petr\nChalupaおよび1名の匿名査読者が査読を行った。<\/p>\n"}], "pages": [[595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062], [595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062], [595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062], [595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062], [595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062], [595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062], [595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062], [595.2755737304688, 785.1968383789062]], "translation_status": "ready", "model": "pfnet/plamo-3-translate-2b"}